module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_refusal_reason_and_its_class_are_paired_by_hand

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyImpossible }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// A REFUSAL CARRIES TWO FACTS THAT MUST AGREE, AND THE TYPE LETS THEM DISAGREE. The reason names which
// decision answered no; the class says what kind of refusal that is, and it decides which diagnostic an
// author is shown. A record that takes both as independent fields pairs them at every construction site,
// and a wrong pair is a well-typed value.
data a_refusal_reason_and_its_class_are_paired_by_hand: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_refusal_reason_and_its_class_are_paired_by_hand" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: StructurallyImpossible, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the capability of compiling and validating the affected production sites (v2.std.inhabitance, v2.compiler.infer) together with the 15 claim-site consumers that match InhabitanceRefused, under an authorized route, and of EXECUTING those claims wherever behavioural evidence is required. Required CI compiles the production closures and omits the claim modules, so a change to a refusal's class, or a consumer that stops seeing a field of it, is checked on one side of the pair only." } },

  receipts: [
    "**a pair of fields that must agree, with nothing making them agree, is one fact with many producers.** gunbc.design_argument::single_authority: one fact decided in more than one place is a fork, and the fact here is what kind of refusal this is -- produced at each construction site instead of read from the decision that made it. gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed asks that a wrong answer be unwritable, or typed, located and countable; a mismatched pair is neither, because it is just a value.",

    "INVALID STATE, THE VIOLATED INVARIANT: one decision answers no and the verdict it returns carries find_witness_reason: Symbol and refusal_class: InhabitanceRefusalClass as two independent fields (the InhabitanceRefused arm of InhabitanceVerdict, src/v2/std/inhabitance.dag). The invariant is that a reason and its class name the same decision. Nothing in the type enforces it: ^inhabitance_comparison_candidate_malformed beside RefusalStructuralMismatch is a well-typed value, and so is any other mismatch.",

    "EVERY SITE THAT PAIRS, at the head this row is written on. Hand-written pairs, three, all in src/v2/std/inhabitance.dag: declared_type_inhabitance (an Optional produced where a required value is declared), inhabitance_optional_layer_verdict (the malformed-wrapper answer), and inhabitance_optional_layer_depth_mismatch_refusal (the depth-mismatch refusal, which the OptionalLayerDepthMismatch arm of inhabitance_optional_layer_verdict and the Absent arm of declared_type_inhabitance_optional now share). Sites that FORWARD a class decided elsewhere, two, both in the same module: declared_type_inhabitance_refusal and inhabitance_decision_through_argument, each taking refusal_class from an InhabitanceStructuralDecision. And the ONE classifier over the structural family, inhabitance_structural_decision, exhaustive with no default arm. Before this row's fix commit the hand-written count was four -- three inside declared_type_inhabitance and one inside inhabitance_with_payloads -- and two of them named the same fact twice; the count is now three, one per decision. That is the mitigation, and it is not the guarantee.",

    "HARM AND CONSEQUENCE: the class is not decoration. inhabitance_refusal_diagnostic sends RefusalStructuralMismatch and RefusalWitnessSearchDecision to application_argument_does_not_inhabit_diagnostic, which carries a SUGGESTED NODE, and RefusalComparisonCouldNotRun to inhabitance_refusal_without_suggestion_diagnostic, which carries none. A mismatched pair therefore sends an author to fix a type error the compiler never showed. The cost of staying below the ceiling is that the next reason added at a new site can be paired with the wrong class and nothing refuses it -- which is not hypothetical, see the SPECIMEN.",

    "SPECIMEN, review 92072 at ffd4e4ec: the malformed-optional-wrapper arm paired ^inhabitance_optional_layer_wrapper_malformed with RefusalStructuralMismatch, while the classifier in the same module puts every malformed input in RefusalComparisonCouldNotRun and describes that family as never a claim that the value's type is wrong. A malformed occupancy wrapper is an input that is not a well-formed node, so the shipped pair contradicted its own module, and the author-facing diagnostic offered a suggested fix for a type error that did not exist. The fix commit this row is written on decides the class once, inside the layer judgement, and shares one construction between the two depth-mismatch routes. Its discriminators are v2.test.claim.compiler.optional_layers a_malformed_occupancy_wrapper_refuses_as_could_not_run and a_malformed_occupancy_wrapper_diagnostic_carries_no_suggested_node, with a_depth_mismatch_keeps_the_type_mismatch_class_and_its_suggestion and an_optional_at_a_required_declared_position_keeps_the_type_mismatch_class as controls. Those five rows are UNEXECUTED PREDICTIONS: required CI does not compile claim modules (gunbc.rung_drop) and no claim run has been granted for them.",

    "PRESENT RUNG: mitigatable -- the class is decided where the fact is known, each (reason, class) pair is written exactly once in the module, and the classifier over the structural family is exhaustive with no default arm. CEILING: structurally impossible -- with the reason as a closed sum whose arms carry the class (InhabitanceRefusalReason = RefusalReasonWitnessSearchDecision { reason } | RefusalReasonComparisonCouldNotRun { reason } | RefusalReasonStructuralMismatch { reason }; InhabitanceRefused { reason: InhabitanceRefusalReason, position }; refusal_class deleted and read from the arm), a mismatched pair has no constructor at all. The distance between the rung and the ceiling is unbuilt work, not a limit of the language.",

    "ACCOUNTABLE OWNER: session valiant-deer-27, managed by tidy-ant-251, on gunb-ai/gunbc#15868. This row is the deferral's carrier, not a waiver: it does not say the pair is safe today, and it does not claim the mitigation catches a future mismatch. It says the pair is mis-pairable, someone owns closing that, and the next change that touches it must read this row.",

    "CAPABILITY TRIGGER, named as a capability and not as a date: the affected production sites (v2.std.inhabitance, v2.compiler.infer) and the 15 claim-site consumers that match InhabitanceRefused can be COMPILED and validated under an authorized route, and EXECUTED where behavioural evidence is required. Required CI omits those consumers today: the v2-bootstrap job compiles the production closures, and claim modules are not in the emitted closures (gunbc.rung_drop). That is exactly why the closed-sum migration is deferred beside this fix instead of landed inside it -- the migration rewrites 5 production match sites and 15 claim-site matches, and at this head the second group cannot be checked by any granted route, so the change would trade a typed defect for an unverified edit.",

    "PLANNED MIGRATION AND RE-REVIEW CHECKPOINT, so the deferral cannot close silently: the migration is the ceiling shape above, landed as its own change with (a) the claim-site census re-derived at that head, (b) the five optional_layers rows and every existing refusal row re-pinned against the new shape, and (c) a fresh exact-head review of that change. Until it lands, this row carries the class and its rung reads mitigatable-below-ceiling, not at-ceiling.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
